      "writtenOn": "2022-08-31T03:20:50Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Re Enshuo:\n\nI think it\u0027s possible to log \"a2dp supported\" when the headset never claimed A2DP connection, I intended to fix one cause of that in aosp/2191601.\n\n`selectable_caps` is used to decide if a2dp is supported (see ~L383 in that patch), but it is not cleared when previous headset is removed.\n\nSo I guess if the previous headset claims a2dp supported, then HM* will claim that and log it anyway...\n\nI\u0027m trying to fix that along with this patch, and I also find the cap added/removed logic to be more tricky than I initially thought (especially now we have 3 profiles and proactive connections): e.g., I saw a headset acting weird and adding/removing AVRCP within the 5s frame.",
      "parentUuid": "ff51d905_d276b583",
      "range": {
